<%--
Document_Preview

Renders a real, in-browser preview of a file attachment by resolving a viewer component from the
server (File_Preview_Controller::get_preview_info) and dispatching to it. The framework ships three
viewers (Pdf_Viewer, Image_Viewer, Icon_Viewer); an app may register additional viewers in
config('rsx.preview.viewers'), which are instantiated dynamically in on_ready.

A convertible document (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, ...) has no PDF rendition until the background
render worker has produced one, so this component also owns the WAITING states: it subscribes to
its attachment id and swaps from "Preparing preview..." to the real Pdf_Viewer when the render
lands - no reload, no polling.

States, in the order the template tests them:
  preview_unavailable  - a degraded upload (unparseable image bytes). No viewer.
  render_status_id 2   - PENDING: queued for render. "Preparing preview..." + the extension icon.
  render_status_id 4   - FAILED: terminal. "Preview could not be generated" + the extension icon.
                         The operator reason (render_error) is deliberately NOT exported here.
  urls.rendition       - a PDF (its own blob) or a RENDERED convertible document -> Pdf_Viewer.
  otherwise            - Image_Viewer / Icon_Viewer / an app-registered viewer.

Args:
  $attachment_id  (required) - the File_Attachment_Model id to preview. Throws if absent.
  $page           (optional) - initial page for paginated viewers (default 1).
  $width/$height  (optional) - fixed dimensions in px; omitted -> fills the container (100%).
  $fit            (optional) - how a paginated page is scaled inside the frame:
                    "width"   (default) scale to the frame's WIDTH; a portrait page overflows
                              vertically and the frame scrolls. Unchanged behaviour.
                    "contain" scale so the WHOLE page is visible:
                              min(frame_width/page_width, frame_height/page_height).
                              REQUIRES A HOST WITH BOUNDED HEIGHT - $height, or a host element
                              with a real height - since that is what the fit divides by. Given
                              none (height:auto), it falls back to the width fit.
                  Any other value throws. Only paginated viewers act on it; Image_Viewer and
                  Icon_Viewer already fit both axes and are not given it.

  A paginated viewer also re-renders the current page when the frame changes size (debounced), so
  a pane that grows re-rasters at the new size instead of stretching the old bitmap.

Events OUT (re-emitted from the active viewer):
  'preview_loaded' {pages, width, height, ratio}  - width/height/ratio describe the page CURRENTLY
                                                   RENDERED, not the document, so on a mixed-
                                                   orientation file they change with the page.
                                                  (NOT 'loaded' - that is a reserved jqhtml
                                                   lifecycle event fired internally with no data)
  'page_changed'   {page}

Public methods (delegate to the active viewer; no-op before it is ready):
  set_page(n) / get_page() / get_pages()
--%>
<Define:Document_Preview tag="div">
    <% if (!this.args.attachment_id) { throw new Error('Document_Preview requires $attachment_id'); } %>
    <%
        const _w = this.args.width ? (int(this.args.width) + 'px') : '100%';
        const _h = this.args.height ? (int(this.args.height) + 'px') : '100%';
        const _frame_style = 'width:' + _w + ';height:' + _h + ';';
    %>
    <div class="Document_Preview__frame" style="<%= _frame_style %>">
        <% if (this.data.info && this.data.info.preview_unavailable) { %>
            <%-- Degraded upload (image bytes were unparseable): no viewer is instantiated, so
                 on_ready finds no $sid="viewer" component and no-ops. --%>
            <div class="Document_Preview__unavailable">
                <img class="Document_Preview__unavailable-icon" src="<%= this.data.info.urls.icon %>" alt="">
                <div class="Document_Preview__unavailable-title">Preview unavailable</div>
                <% if (this.data.info.file_name) { %>
                    <div class="Document_Preview__unavailable-name"><%= this.data.info.file_name %></div>
                <% } %>
            </div>
        <% } else if (this.data.info && this.data.info.render_status_id === 2) { %>
            <%-- PENDING: the render worker has the document queued. The realtime subscription in
                 on_create brings us back here the moment it finishes. --%>
            <div class="Document_Preview__preparing">
                <img class="Document_Preview__state-icon" src="<%= this.data.info.urls.icon %>" alt="">
                <div class="Document_Preview__state-title">Preparing preview...</div>
                <% if (this.data.info.file_name) { %>
                    <div class="Document_Preview__state-name"><%= this.data.info.file_name %></div>
                <% } %>
            </div>
        <% } else if (this.data.info && this.data.info.render_status_id === 4) { %>
            <%-- FAILED is terminal - nothing retries it but an operator (rsx:documents:rerender). --%>
            <div class="Document_Preview__failed">
                <img class="Document_Preview__state-icon" src="<%= this.data.info.urls.icon %>" alt="">
                <div class="Document_Preview__state-title">Preview could not be generated</div>
                <% if (this.data.info.file_name) { %>
                    <div class="Document_Preview__state-name"><%= this.data.info.file_name %></div>
                <% } %>
            </div>
        <% } else if (this.data.info) { %>
            <% const _v = this.data.info.viewer; %>
            <% if (_v === 'Pdf_Viewer' && this.data.info.urls.rendition) { %>
                <Pdf_Viewer $sid="viewer" $url=this.data.info.urls.rendition $page=(this.args.page||1) $fit=this.args.fit />
            <% } else if (_v === 'Pdf_Viewer') { %>
                <%-- Resolves to Pdf_Viewer but has no rendition and is in no render state that
                     explains why (a blob that was never materialized). Fall through to the icon
                     rather than handing the viewer a null URL. --%>
                <Icon_Viewer $sid="viewer" $url=this.data.info.urls.icon $extension=this.data.info.extension $file_name=this.data.info.file_name />
            <% } else if (_v === 'Image_Viewer') { %>
                <Image_Viewer $sid="viewer" $url=this.data.info.urls.inline />
            <% } else if (_v === 'Icon_Viewer') { %>
                <Icon_Viewer $sid="viewer" $url=this.data.info.urls.icon $extension=this.data.info.extension $file_name=this.data.info.file_name />
            <% } else { %>
                <div $sid="viewer" class="Document_Preview__dynamic"></div>
            <% } %>
        <% } %>
    </div>
</Define:Document_Preview>
